# 0007 plugin: bounded first-failure journal for the Metal-on-Vulkan path
#
# Base:  this patch series, after 0006 (XeMTL plugin tree)
# Files: plugin/nvmtl_first_loss.h (new)
#        plugin/NVMTLObjects.m, plugin/nvmtl_vk.c, plugin/nvmtl_vk.h, plugin/XeMTLDevice.m (modified)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0007-plugin-first-loss-journal.patch
#
# The plugin has no second chance after a Vulkan submit closes the backend, so the first failure
# has to be recorded before it is overwritten.  The journal writes one JSON line per event (submit
# begin/end, fence waits, bind-sparse, host-pointer import, image binding) to a bounded file, marks
# the backend down exactly once, and preserves the Vulkan driver's own error text through syslog.
# It is opt-in: set XEMTL_FIRST_LOSS_TRACE=1, or create /private/tmp/xemtl-first-loss-enable as
# root so a launchd-started WindowServer picks it up; the log goes to
# $XEMTL_FIRST_LOSS_DIR/xemtl-first-loss-<pid>.jsonl (default /private/tmp).  The same sentinel
# also sets XEMTL_DRM_TRACE=1 for the libdrm ioctl trace in that process.
# This tree also carries the no-wait submit branch and the per-call timing counters (census) that were used to
# find the compositor stall, which is why NVMTLObjects.m and larger parts of nvmtl_vk.c differ from the
# first-journal-only version.
#

--- a/plugin/NVMTLObjects.m
+++ b/plugin/NVMTLObjects.m
